questions.question_text:
$X$ is uniformly distributed on $[1,9]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0) -- (6.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (1,0) -- (1,2) -- (5,2) -- (5,0);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$9$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Find the mean and the variance of $X$.

questions.solution_text:
$\mu=\frac{1+9}{2}$
$=5$
$\sigma^{2}=\frac{(9-1)^{2}}{12}$
$=\frac{64}{12}$
$=\frac{16}{3}$
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[-{Stealth}] (-0.5,0) -- (6.2,0) node[right] {$x$};
\draw[-{Stealth}] (0,-0.4) -- (0,3.0) node[above] {$y$};
\draw[thick] (1,0) -- (1,2) -- (5,2) -- (5,0);
\draw[dashed] (3,0) -- (3,2);
\node[below] at (1,0) {$1$};
\node[below] at (5,0) {$9$};
\node[above right] at (3,2) {$\mu=5$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

